    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2561b03f"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Prevailing Crime Type in the Second Half of the Data\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on the previous analysis, the dataset was divided into two halves to assess crime rate trends. Now, we will focus on the second half to identify the most common type of crime during that period."
      ],
      "id": "2561b03f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "b4455604",
        "outputId": "88f9dd6b-d0cd-4c4e-99d3-ef090ca3c73a"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Get the start date of the second half from the daily_crime_counts index\n",
        "if len(daily_crime_counts) > 0:\n",
        "    second_half_start_date = daily_crime_counts.index[len(daily_crime_counts) // 2]\n",
        "    print(f\"The second half of the data for crime analysis starts from: {second_half_start_date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Filter the crimes DataFrame to include only the second half\n",
        "    crimes_second_half = crimes[crimes['DATE OCC'] >= second_half_start_date]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Determine the most prevailing type of crime in this second half\n",
        "    if not crimes_second_half.empty:\n",
        "        prevailing_crime_second_half = crimes_second_half['Crm Cd Desc'].mode()[0]\n",
        "        prevailing_crime_count = crimes_second_half['Crm Cd Desc'].value_counts().max()\n",
        "        print(f\"\\nThe prevailing type of crime in the second half (where average crime was {second_half_avg:.2f}) is: '{prevailing_crime_second_half}' with {prevailing_crime_count} occurrences.\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(\"No crime data found in the second half to determine prevailing type.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"Cannot determine prevailing crime type as there is no daily crime data available.\")"
      ],
      "id": "b4455604",
      "execution_count": 28,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "The second half of the data for crime analysis starts from: 2021-08-19\n",
            "\n",
            "The prevailing type of crime in the second half (where average crime was 42.11) is: 'THEFT OF IDENTITY' with 2935 occurrences.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "af406e7b"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Time of Day Analysis for Crimes\n",
        "\n",
        "Now, let's determine the time when most and least crimes occur by analyzing the 'TIME OCC' column."
      ],
      "id": "af406e7b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 661
        },
        "id": "9e7982c8",
        "outputId": "fc847372-0fe3-46f5-8007-caf07e9fd65a"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Ensure 'TIME OCC' is treated as string for consistency then convert to integer hour\n",
        "# Pad with leading zeros if necessary to ensure 4 digits, then extract hour\n",
        "crimes['TIME OCC'] = crimes['TIME OCC'].astype(str).str.zfill(4)\n",
        "crimes['HOUR OCC'] = crimes['TIME OCC'].str[:2].astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Count crimes per hour\n",
        "hourly_crime_counts = crimes['HOUR OCC'].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plotting hourly crime distribution\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "hourly_crime_counts.plot(kind='bar', color='coral')\n",
        "plt.title('Number of Crimes by Hour of Day')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Hour of Day (24-hour format)')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Number of Crimes')\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
        "plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Find the time when most crimes occur\n",
        "most_common_hour = hourly_crime_counts.idxmax()\n",
        "max_crimes = hourly_crime_counts.max()\n",
        "print(f\"\\nThe hour with the most crimes is {most_common_hour:02d}:00 (with {max_crimes} crimes).\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Find the time when least crimes occur\n",
        "least_common_hour = hourly_crime_counts.idxmin()\n",
        "min_crimes = hourly_crime_counts.min()\n",
        "print(f\"The hour with the least crimes is {least_common_hour:02d}:00 (with {min_crimes} crimes).\")"
      ],
      "id": "9e7982c8",
      "execution_count": 29,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "The hour with the most crimes is 12:00 (with 1924 crimes).\n",
            "The hour with the least crimes is 05:00 (with 360 crimes).\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "830c17cb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Prevailing Crime Types at Specific Hours (Noon and 5 AM)\n",
        "\n",
        "Now, let's drill down into the crime types that are most common during the peak crime hour (noon) and the hour with the least crimes (5 AM)."
      ],
      "id": "830c17cb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3d2bc522",
        "outputId": "4c593a7f-b7c1-43e6-ba50-528b67a543fd"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Prevailing crime at 12:00 (noon)\n",
        "crimes_noon = crimes[crimes['HOUR OCC'] == 12]\n",
        "if not crimes_noon.empty:\n",
        "    prevailing_crime_noon = crimes_noon['Crm Cd Desc'].mode()[0]\n",
        "    count_noon = crimes_noon['Crm Cd Desc'].value_counts().max()\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nThe prevailing type of crime at 12:00 (noon) is: '{prevailing_crime_noon}' with {count_noon} occurrences.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"No crimes recorded at 12:00 (noon).\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Prevailing crime at 05:00 (5 AM)\n",
        "crimes_5am = crimes[crimes['HOUR OCC'] == 5]\n",
        "if not crimes_5am.empty:\n",
        "    prevailing_crime_5am = crimes_5am['Crm Cd Desc'].mode()[0]\n",
        "    count_5am = crimes_5am['Crm Cd Desc'].value_counts().max()\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nThe prevailing type of crime at 05:00 (5 AM) is: '{prevailing_crime_5am}' with {count_5am} occurrences.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"No crimes recorded at 05:00 (5 AM).\")"
      ],
      "id": "3d2bc522",
      "execution_count": 31,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
